{
  "case_id": "2012-11-864",
  "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Estrada, you are limiting your argument to the determination of damages, as I understand it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ESTRADA: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Third Circuit held in this case that the assessment of the adequacy of expert evidence offered in support of class certification is a merits question that has no place in the class certification inquiry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But why -- why not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ESTRADA: Well, let me make two points in response to that question, Justice Ginsburg: One about what the legal standards are, and -- you know, the second one, which is as important, about what the record in this case is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ESTRADA: But, Justice Kagan, I mean, I think we could go through chapter and verse to everything that we put in the reply brief. But I think, in fairness, I have to point out to you that we never said that our objection was to the weight and not to the admissibility."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Estrada, could you pronounce for me or give me the legal rule as you want us to articulate it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ESTRADA: No, we did not, and we actually don't think that that's needed because it would actually be sort of silly to engage in a motion to strike the evidence that we are asking the district judge to consider, in order to decide whether it actually is reliable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Barnett",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And to get a sense of how profoundly uninterested Comcast was in Daubert and in arguing weight and probativeness, as opposed to admissibility, which is the question before this Court, they never, ever cited Daubert. They didn't cite it in the district court. They didn't cite it in the court of appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Barnett, it's always true, isn't it, that evidence that is inadequately probative is inadmissible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I am still in search of a legal question that anybody disagrees about here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Comcast",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The parties both agree with that statement of the standard. It seems to me that the parties also both agree -- and this goes back to Justice Sotomayor's question -- that if the Daubert question had not been waived, that if -- if Comcast had objected to the admissibility of this expert report, that, indeed, the court would -- should have held a hearing on the admissibility of the expert report."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, before you do that, let me ask a question related to what Justice Kagan just asked. If we were to answer the question presented as reformulated, I take it your answer would be that a district court under those circumstances may not certify a class action; is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, then the only remaining question is whether the issue was in the case as a factual -- as a matter of the record here; isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, tell me -- you articulate for me what you think -- what the district court found when it accepted your expert's theory as adequate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Comcast",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What Judge Padova found was that the McClave damages model is persuasive to him -- sufficiently persuasive to him, that it could be used at trial to prove damages on a class-wide basis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Barnett, this is on a different issue, but you had originally suggested that you had -- that the motion -- that the settlement that's looming was a reason that this Court ought not to decide this case. But do you now agree that, given the district court's denial of your motion to enforce the settlement, that the proposed settlement has no bearing on this Court's consideration of the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a6bd468829792f69ddc2b30677723638f86b5b263ad5e297b984a931600bb30",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a6bd4688297-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is that right? Is that what Learned Hand said? Is -- is that what Alcoa holds? Is that United Fruit holds when they bomb their competitor's ship and achieve monopolization?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-11-864",
      "confidence": 0.0,
